title the population a guard reads -- the citation scan asks the card what prose is, and %398 closes at its root
prompt The HUSH seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5 advancing by hand past a repeat, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves, claim-as-override when my lane's queue is empty. My own last recommend named %398 as the sharper of two findings and left it for its owner.
think LISTAGENTS FIRST answered none reachable, so /proc cwd named the peers. One pass was running that was not mine -- standing_equipment_run.sh --hot, 23 minutes in, cwd /home/keeper/grain-dream. Dream, in Dream's own tree, closing Dream's own lap. Nothing of mine moves there and nothing of theirs is mine to touch. The opening stash held one untracked file, caravan/.suite-runtime/lock.d/pid, a stale suite lock rather than lost work, and it stays where it is.
think ROTA ROW 1 AGAIN, SO I ADVANCED BY HAND TO ROW 2 as the seed's own paragraph permits. N = git rev-list --count HEAD = 3881, 3881 mod 5 = 1, and the previous lap read row 1 -- the repeat case the grid's own measurement counts among two in nineteen pairs. Row 2 is FIRE, cut and stop: the threshold, then standfast, reds-first, and the three depths of removal. The row and the lap met exactly, which is rarer than it sounds and worth naming rather than admiring.
think THE STANDFAST WAS ALREADY WRITTEN AND IT WAS MINE TO PLACE. %398 stood OPEN, gated at zero, and its own row says every body's roster pass closes guard_red until it is repaired. My last lap booked it and left it to %392's owner. A day passed, xy did not move, nobody took it, and it was blocking my own lane's ability to earn a green receipt. Reds-first orders the constructive queue and standfast halts the line, so the line halted here.
think I REPRODUCED BEFORE I READ THE CODE. sh tools/fixtures/c/comment_citation_scan.sh reads 108 programs, 10 broken, verdict=broken_citation, 41s -- the same ten my last lap proved on two worktrees. Every one sits in a dated .kyri log, and reading their actual lines rather than trusting the list confirmed the classes item for item: `](./x.md)` and `](../REDS.md)` inside backticks, [`kumara.rye`](kumara.rye) and [`name.rye`](name.rye) as bare filenames, 32000 and -32768 as index-then-value arithmetic.
think THE ROOT IS ONE CASE STATEMENT AND IT IS NOT WHERE MY LAST LAP POINTED. %392's repair added `*.bron|*.kyri` to TWO lists in qa_report_card.sh -- artifact_kind AND truth_source -- and the second is the one that bites. A file read as truth_source=prose gets neither the awk backtick strip nor the looks-like-a-path filter, because both are gated on truth_source=comments. Meanwhile the scan's own candidate filter still spells ':!*.md' ':!*.mdc' ':!*.markdown' and has never heard of the notations. Two spellings of one class, drifted apart.
think SO THE EXCLUSIONS WERE NEVER THE THING TO MOVE. My own row proposed moving the four exclusions to whichever card function now emits unresolved:. That would change the Truth reading for every .md document the card grades, which is the blast radius the card's own comment explicitly scoped out -- a fenced-block rule reaches 20+ documents and wants its own round. The narrow fix is the population, and the population is the scan's.
think AND THE DECISIVE ARGUMENT IS A LAW RATHER THAN A PREFERENCE. All ten broken citations sit in dated session logs. Dated testimony keeps every word it wrote, so the only repair available to close a gate of zero was an edit accrete-never-break forbids. A guard whose only available repair is forbidden can never go green, and that is not a fact about phrasing -- it is a proof that the guard was reading the wrong population.
think THE CONTROL ALREADY HELD THE PRINCIPLE FOR ONE SPELLING AND NOT THE OTHER. Case 9 plants a .md with a broken link and proves the scan stays green -- prose is another guard's population, said out loud on 20260825. It was proven for .md and never for the notations, because on that day the card did not call them prose either. The drift walked straight through the gap between one proven spelling and one unproven one.
obs THE REPAIR IS THAT THE SCAN ASKS RATHER THAN ANSWERS. It now captures the card's whole output once per candidate -- the same single invocation it already paid for -- reads truth_source= out of it, and skips what the card calls prose. Counted as prose_skipped rather than dropped: a skip nobody can see cannot be told from a guard that stopped reading. Reads programs_scanned=95 prose_skipped=13 broken_citations=0 verdict=ok, and 95 + 13 is the same 108, so nothing vanished.
obs THE PREFILTER STAYS, AND ITS INVARIANT IS NOW PROVEN RATHER THAN ASSUMED. The git grep keeps its .md exclusions for speed, since running the card over every tracked document costs minutes and a guard nobody waits for is a guard somebody skips. What changed is that correctness no longer rests on that second list: control case 13 runs the card on a probe of each dropped extension plus both notations and asserts every one reads truth_source=prose. That is the case that would have caught this on the lap it entered.
obs PROVEN FROM BOTH SIDES ON A WORKTREE OF THE UNREPAIRED SCAN. I checked out HEAD detached, copied the NEW control over the OLD scan, and ran it: prose_notation_skipped=no, prose_skip_counted=no, same_target_removed_returns_green=no. Two readings stayed yes and that is correct rather than a weakness -- same_target_in_program_bitten never depended on the repair, and prefilter_matches_card_prose reads the card's side of an invariant only the scan had broken. A control whose new cases all pass against the unrepaired code would have proven nothing.
obs THE SKIP TURNS ON CLASS, NEVER ON CONTENT, AND THE CONTROL SAYS SO. Case 12 plants the identical broken target inside a .rye and asserts it still refuses and still names the program, then removes it and asserts the reading returns to green. Without that pair the repair would be indistinguishable from a guard that learned to stop reading.
obs ONE NEAR-MISS I CHECKED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. A program's own card line reads truth_source=comments (a program cites in its comments; a prose file cites everywhere) -- so the bare word prose appears in EVERY reading the scan takes, and only anchoring the pattern to truth_source=prose tells the two apart. I ran it both directions on metal before writing the comment that says so.
obs I NAMED WHAT THE SKIP LEAVES OPEN RATHER THAN LETTING A READER FIND IT. tracked_link_scan.sh reads .md alone, so a citation inside a LIVING .kyri or .bron is now read by neither guard. Measured: 4,080 tracked such files, 13 carry `](`, and all 13 are dated -- the gap holds zero living files today. Named in the scan header with its measurement, since a bounded coverage nobody logs reads as coverage.
obs MY OWN SLIP COST A FORTY-MINUTE PASS ON A SHARED FOUR-CORE BOX, AND IT IS MINE TO OWN. The card says roster cold then hot and hold still while it runs, and the runner digests the WHOLE tree -- staged, unstaged and untracked alike -- at open and at close. I opened the cold pass and then edited six files while it ran, which fixed its verdict at tree_moved 26 minutes in, with Dream holding a pass on the same four vCPUs. A cold pass and an editing lap are serial, never parallel. I ended my own pass with TERM rather than letting a void reading hold the lock for another quarter hour; the trap released it clean, and killing my own pass is not the cross-hand act %291 forbids. Not booked as a red: the guard caught it exactly as designed and nothing in the tree is wrong. The cost is named here so the next lap serializes.
obs QA ON TOUCH PUSHED NO FRAME, AND THE ONE GRADE THAT MOVED WENT UP FOR AN HONEST REASON. The scan read B 83 before I named the open gap and B+ 87 after -- register 52 to 56, reach 80 to 90 -- because the added paragraph is plain affirmative prose and lifted both counted readings. Control A 93, witness B+ 85. Adding an honest paragraph raising a grade is the opposite of the %397 shape, where punctuation moved a grade with content unchanged, and both are the same lesson about what the formula actually reads.
obs I FOLDED CAUSE AND COST ONTO ONE SHELF. %392 is Silence's and CLOSED, %398 is mine and now CLOSED, and apart they read as two small repairs while together they teach one thing -- a reader that cites an instrument is a reader that reruns when the instrument moves. reds_fold.sh moved both, links reanchored, recital written; the pin fell 24,730 over its wall to 17,375 with 7,201 free, and the monotone spine reads headline_span=398 disagreements=0.
obs THE CITING POPULATION IS CLOSED AT ONE, WHICH I MEASURED RATHER THAN HOPED. Twelve living files name qa_report_card, and the only ones that RUN it are this scan and the card's own witness. The two Pond fixtures cite it as precedent in a comment -- pond_enclosure_ephemeral_scan.sh lifts a tokenizer the way the card lifts measure() -- and neither invokes it, so neither carries this drift.
obs THE REPAIR PROVED ITSELF ON ITS OWN RECORD, WITHIN THE HOUR, WITHOUT MY ARRANGING IT. This log quotes the four broken shapes to explain them -- `](./x.md)`, `](../REDS.md)`, [`kumara.rye`](kumara.rye), [`name.rye`](name.rye) -- so it is itself a dated .kyri carrying link syntax. Run through the card it reads truth_source=prose with 4 of 4 cited paths unresolved. Under the UNREPAIRED scan this very log would have carried the guard from 10 broken to 14 on the lap that closed the row; under the repair it is read as prose and skipped, and the tree's reading is prose_skipped=14 rather than the 13 I measured before writing it. A guard that reds on the document explaining why it reds is the clearest statement of a wrong population I could have hoped to find, and I did not have to construct it.
obs THE COUNTS IN THE LEDGER ROW AND THE SCAN HEADER STAY AS THEY WERE WRITTEN, because both are stamped readings. `20260831.085457` measured 13, and a figure carries its date -- the tree gains files hourly, and a measurement that must be edited whenever the tree grows is a measurement nobody can trust. The card's live clause moved to the invariant instead: every candidate is read or counted, none is dropped.
obs THE HOT PASS IS THE READING, AND THE COLD ONE I VOIDED IS NOT MOURNED. 108 guards, 107 green, ONE red, tree_moved=no over the 9 staged paths, 1,714 guard-seconds. The one red is `rule_twin` -- custody gate %7, standing on Keaton's word, where 38 of 39 drifted rule pairs are two-way and a bulk merge would silently delete a live safety rule. Every other guard that was red on my last lap now reads green, and I proved the four candidates one at a time rather than inferring from a truncated tail: `comment_citation` GREEN, `geode_libraries` GREEN, `nib_honesty` GREEN, `remember_git_nib` green in the pass itself.
